        "description": "Pixels show one upper rounded planar patch labelled alpha and one lower rounded patch labelled beta. The two patches have the same broad horizontal orientation, with M inside alpha and N inside beta. No right-angle, equal-length, grid, numeric or dimension marks are printed. Modern regularization: congruent projected circular patches replace irregular scan outlines; these are schematic windows onto infinite planes, not solid disks.",
