      },
      {
        "id": "source-line-points-and-direction",
        "description": "Pixels show one vertical line a, labelled a above alpha; solid from above alpha to the filled dot M, dashed from M to the lower alpha rim, solid between patches with one downward arrowhead ending at the filled dot N, dashed from N to the lower beta rim, and solid continuing below beta. M is above N and both lie on the same line. The arrow encodes the proof translation MN, not two endpoint arrows. No other source point, arrow, or line is present. Caption is outside the instructional image and is supplied by the lesson.",
